Simpler: use NSRegularExpression to find all matches of `#([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)`.

```swift
public func extractTags(from text: String) -> [String] {
    let pattern = try! NSRegularExpression(pattern: "#([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)")
    let range = NSRange(text.startIndex..., in: text)
    return pattern.matches(in: text, range: range)
        .compactMap { m in
            guard let r = Range(m.range(1), in: text) else { return nil }
            return String(text[r])
        }
}
```

Order is preserved (NSRegularExpression returns matches in order). Note: `#` is literal
, no problem. `#` at the start of a line — no word-boundary requirement, so no problem
.

Edge cases: `#urgent` in `list,#urgent.` — matches `urgent`. `(#ideas)` — matches
 `ideas`. `hello #world #swift` → `world`, `swift`. Plain text → `[]`. `#a#b` → `
a`, `b`.

